### Rating System Validation Tests
### These tests validate the rating calculation system after review operations

@baseUrl = {{$dotenv BACKEND_URL}}
@authToken = {{$dotenv AUTH_TOKEN}}
@productId = {{$dotenv PRODUCT_ID}}
@reviewId = 

### Variables (Update these with actual values)
# Set these environment variables or replace directly:
# BACKEND_URL=http://localhost:5000/api
# AUTH_TOKEN=your_jwt_token
# PRODUCT_ID=valid_product_id

###
### 1. Get Initial Rating Summary
GET {{baseUrl}}/product/{{productId}}/rating-summary
Content-Type: application/json

###
### 2. Validate Rating Consistency Before Operations
GET {{baseUrl}}/review/validate-consistency/{{productId}}
Content-Type: application/json

###
### 3. Create a Review (Rating: 5)
POST {{baseUrl}}/review/addReview
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "productId": "{{productId}}",
  "rating": 5,
  "comment": "Excellent product! Highly recommended."
}

###
### 4. Validate Consistency After Creation
GET {{baseUrl}}/review/validate-consistency/{{productId}}
Content-Type: application/json

###
### 5. Get Updated Rating Summary
GET {{baseUrl}}/product/{{productId}}/rating-summary
Content-Type: application/json

###
### 6. Create Another Review (Rating: 3)
POST {{baseUrl}}/review/addReview
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "productId": "{{productId}}",
  "rating": 3,
  "comment": "Average product. Could be better."
}

###
### 7. Validate Consistency After Second Review
GET {{baseUrl}}/review/validate-consistency/{{productId}}
Content-Type: application/json

###
### 8. Get Updated Rating Summary
GET {{baseUrl}}/product/{{productId}}/rating-summary
Content-Type: application/json

###
### 9. Update First Review (Change rating from 5 to 4)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/review/updateReview/{{reviewId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "rating": 4,
  "comment": "Good product. Updated my review."
}

###
### 10. Validate Consistency After Update
GET {{baseUrl}}/review/validate-consistency/{{productId}}
Content-Type: application/json

###
### 11. Get Rating Summary After Update
GET {{baseUrl}}/product/{{productId}}/rating-summary
Content-Type: application/json

###
### 12. Delete a Review
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/review/deleteReview/{{reviewId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

###
### 13. Validate Consistency After Deletion
GET {{baseUrl}}/review/validate-consistency/{{productId}}
Content-Type: application/json

###
### 14. Get Final Rating Summary
GET {{baseUrl}}/product/{{productId}}/rating-summary
Content-Type: application/json

###
### 15. Force Recalculate Ratings (Debug)
POST {{baseUrl}}/review/recalculate-ratings/{{productId}}
Content-Type: application/json

###
### 16. Final Consistency Check
GET {{baseUrl}}/review/validate-consistency/{{productId}}
Content-Type: application/json

###
### Expected Behavior Validation:
### 
### 1. Initial State: avgRating=0, ratingsCount=0, totalReviews=0
### 2. After 1st Review (5⭐): avgRating=5.0, ratingsCount=1, totalReviews=1
### 3. After 2nd Review (3⭐): avgRating=4.0, ratingsCount=2, totalReviews=2
### 4. After Update (5⭐→4⭐): avgRating=3.5, ratingsCount=2, totalReviews=2
### 5. After Delete: avgRating=3.0, ratingsCount=1, totalReviews=1
### 
### Rating Distribution should always match:
### - Count of 1⭐, 2⭐, 3⭐, 4⭐, 5⭐ reviews
### - Sum should equal totalReviews
### 
### All consistency checks should return "isConsistent": true
